HQ verdicts on the seat-48 needs-word list. G7 ruled: NO amending, append-only doctrine bars history rewrite. G11-residual ruled: run the content diff.

G11 REFUTES MY OWN ROW FROM THIS MORNING. zuijdwijk was registered hours ago as 'no code known to be carried', on a Taken-from sweep over arifi/main. Two lane-166 commits carry Taken-from: LaurentZuijdwijk/llama.cpp in full - e146c1175 (matvec NUM_COLS>4 VGPR spill, from 211abf6a9) and c1440b85d (coopmat LDS stride pad, from f97c0e6fe). The sweep read the mainline; the takes were on unmerged branches. A source-registration sweep that only reads the mainline misses every take still in flight - that is the lesson, and it is written into the row rather than quietly corrected. Promoted into sources.json remotes, pinned f97c0e6fe (the later of the two we read and ported), BEHIND by 54 and honestly so.

CONTENT DIFF RUN, arifi/main is CLEAN: patch-id intersection of all 78 zuijdwijk non-upstream commits against all 478 of d7bd3bfca..arifi/main = ZERO verbatim matches. Distinctive-symbol scan (GGML_*/LLAMA_*/--long-opt tokens those 78 add, minus everything already in upstream/master) leaves 46 tokens in our tree, and all 46 are ROCmFPX symbols reaching us via charlie12345/ROCmFPX - a licensed registered source that is also zuijdwijk's own upstream on its qwen4exp-rocmfpx branch. Shared ancestry, not zuijdwijk-originated. Audit assumption 2 was the one named hole in its own coverage; it is now closed for the published branch.

G7: tools/arifi-sync/pending-trailers.json - a DEBT RECORD, not a grant. 550e20479 and 601e3d7a6 classified FORK-NATIVE with evidence (upstream cf2270e4d covers RDNA1/RDNA2 only, so the RDNA3 row cannot be taken from it); f3e13bc94 classified TAKE, and checked rather than assumed - PR #25362 is NOT in upstream/master, so the source must be cited as an UNMERGED pull request, not a sha a reader cannot resolve. On merge-back: paste the trailers, delete the row.

G8 CLOSED as record: the B/C matvec arms ARE committed - lane-166/matvec-vgpr-fix (e146c1175) and lane-166/lds-stride-pad (c1440b85d), one commit each ahead of arifi/main, both fully trailered. The audit's 'ZERO commits ahead' is refuted; it read the branches before they landed. Read-only, no checkout switch.

D1: PUBLISH-DISCLOSURE-DRAFT.md banked as a DRAFT - nothing published, nothing pushed. Leads with FAIL 27, not 315, and says why the old number was real and an artifact.

